TropicalToric -- Macaulay2 package for toric intersection theory using tropical geometry.
*****************************************************************************************

Description
===========

This package implements the computations of classes in the Chow ring of a toric
variety using tropical geometry. Part of this code is based on a package
previously written by Diane Maclagan, Sameera Vemulapalli, Corey Harris, Erika
Pirnes and Ritvik Ramkumar.

Author
======

  * Alessio Borzì (see https://alessioborzi.github.io )
    <Alessio.Borzi@warwick.ac.uk>

Certification a gold star
=========================

Version 1.0 of this package was accepted for publication in volume 14 (see
https://msp.org/jsag/2024/14-1/ ) of Journal of Software for Algebra and
Geometry (see https://msp.org/jsag/ ) on 2023-09-14, in the article Tropical
computations for toric intersection theory in Macaulay2 (see
https://msp.org/jsag/2024/14-1/p04.xhtml ) (DOI: 10.2140/jsag.2024.14.19 (see
https://doi.org/10.2140/jsag.2024.14.19 )). That version can be obtained from
the journal (see https://msp.org/jsag/2024/14-1/jsag-v14-n1-x04-TropicalToric.
zip ).

