classFromTropical -- compute a toric cycle of X which class is the same as a given subvariety of X
**************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        classFromTropical(X,I)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety:
        (NormalToricVarieties)NormalToricVariety,,
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * D, a *note toric cycle: ToricCycle,, 

Description
===========

This function calculates a toric cycle which class is the same of a subvariety
of a normal toric variety X, under the hypothesis that X is simplicial. The
subvariety is given by the ideal of its intersection with the torus inside X.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = toricProjectiveSpace 3;              |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = QQ[x_1 .. x_3];                      |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = ideal(x_1+x_2+x_3+1,x_1+2*x_2-x_3+4);|
|                                              |
|o3 : Ideal of R                               |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : classFromTropical(X,I)                   |
|                                              |
|o4 = X                                        |
|      {0, 1}                                  |
|                                              |
|o4 : ToricCycle on X                          |
+----------------------------------------------+

Ways to use classFromTropical:
==============================

  * "classFromTropical(NormalToricVariety,Ideal)"

