makeTransverse -- Find a divisor linearly equivalent to a toric divisor D that is transverse to a given cone C
**************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        makeTransverse(D,C)
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note toric divisor: (NormalToricVarieties)ToricDivisor,, 
      * C, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * D, a *note toric divisor: (NormalToricVarieties)ToricDivisor,, 

Description
===========

This function calculates a linearly equivalent divisor of a given divisor D
that is transverse to a given cone C.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : rayList={{1,0},{1,1},{0,1},{-1,-1}};                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : coneList={{0,1},{1,2},{2,3},{3,0}};                            |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : X = normalToricVariety fan (transpose matrix rayList,coneList);|
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : D = X_0+X_1;                                                   |
|                                                                    |
|o4 : ToricDivisor on X                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : C = {1,2};                                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isTransverse(D,C)                                              |
|                                                                    |
|o6 = false                                                          |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : makeTransverse(D,C)                                            |
|                                                                    |
|o7 = 2*X  + 0 + 0 + X                                               |
|        0            3                                              |
|                                                                    |
|o7 : ToricDivisor on X                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use makeTransverse:
===========================

  * "makeTransverse(ToricDivisor,List)"

