ToricDivisor * List -- restriction of a Cartier toric divisor to the orbit closure of a cone
********************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note *: (Macaulay2Doc)_st,
  * Usage: 
        D*C
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note toric divisor: (NormalToricVarieties)ToricDivisor,, 
      * C, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note toric cycle: ToricCycle,, Returns the toric cycle given by
        restricting a Cartier toric divisor to the orbit closure of the given
        cone

Description
===========

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : rayList={{1,0},{0,1},{-1,-1},{0,-1}}    |
|                                             |
|o1 = {{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {-1, -1}, {0, -1}}     |
|                                             |
|o1 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : coneList={{0,1},{1,2},{2,3},{3,0}}      |
|                                             |
|o2 = {{0, 1}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}, {3, 0}}        |
|                                             |
|o2 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : X = normalToricVariety(rayList,coneList)|
|                                             |
|o3 = X                                       |
|                                             |
|o3 : NormalToricVariety                      |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : D = X_3                                 |
|                                             |
|o4 = X                                       |
|      3                                      |
|                                             |
|o4 : ToricDivisor on X                       |
+---------------------------------------------+

The only cone containing rays 2 and 3 is the cone {2,3}. There is no cone
containing rows 1 and 3.

+--------------------+
|i5 : D*{2}          |
|                    |
|o5 = X              |
|      {2, 3}        |
|                    |
|o5 : ToricCycle on X|
+--------------------+
|i6 : D*{1}          |
|                    |
|o6 = 0              |
|                    |
|o6 : ToricCycle on X|
+--------------------+

This can also compute more complicated sums.

+------------------------------------+
|i7 : D = X_0 + 2*X_1 + 3*X_2 + 4*X_3|
|                                    |
|o7 = X  + 2*X  + 3*X  + 4*X         |
|      0      1      2      3        |
|                                    |
|o7 : ToricDivisor on X              |
+------------------------------------+
|i8 : C = (orbits X)#1#0             |
|                                    |
|o8 = {0}                            |
|                                    |
|o8 : List                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i9 : D*C                            |
|                                    |
|o9 = 6*X                            |
|        {0, 3}                      |
|                                    |
|o9 : ToricCycle on X                |
+------------------------------------+

